//! Vendored character-width data from upstream `rich`.
//!
//! Generated from `rich._unicode_data`, shipped with rich 15.0.0. Do not edit by
//! hand; regenerate with `scripts/gen_cell_widths.py` when syncing upstream.
//!
//! We previously delegated to the `unicode-width` crate. It disagrees with
//! upstream on 348 code points in a 21,500-point sweep — spacing marks (Mc),
//! format characters (Cf), modifier symbols (Sk) — which misaligned every
//! table, panel and wrap point containing them.
//!
//! All 21 tables upstream ships are here, because `UNICODE_VERSION`
//! selects between them at runtime and a terminal pinned to an older Unicode
//! measures emoji differently from the newest one.

